# `M154b` — the conformance corpus: known-answer plants for tflw's own constructs, graded by
# `scripts/verify-construct-acceptance.mjs` against evidence the plants' targets record themselves.
#
# Its own config root rather than a directory under `perf/`, for two reasons. The first is
# discovery: `scripts/check-acceptance.mjs` walks every directory holding a `tflw.config`, so a new
# corpus is checked from the moment it has one — that script's own header says a hand-maintained
# list is exactly how the last corpus rotted. The second is the target: everything here points at
# `arrival-server.mjs`, a standalone counter with no database and no Docker stack, and pointing it
# at `perf/`'s config would silently make these plants depend on the dogfood stack being up.
env local default
  api "http://127.0.0.1:4507"
